 - **Meshy hero props** arrive unit-normalised (longest side about 1.9). Fit them to the prompt size with `scripts/world/meshy_hero_prop.gd` (`fit_height`), and give painted crystal or lightning veins natural glow with its `glow` next pass (`shaders/blue_vein_glow.gdshader`, blue-dominant texels only).
 - **GPU form for READY lines:** the same tool and arguments with `--rendering-method forward_plus --resolution 1920x1080 --preset=<Medium|High>`. The GPU session captures both arms itself.
 
+**Creature stage and asset lessons (Creatures lane, 25 Oct)**
+- **Stage capture:** `xvfb-run -a -s "-screen 0 1280x720x24" godot --rendering-driver opengl3 --path . --script res://tools/art_pipeline/capture_f36_poses.gd -- --species=<id> --whole-body --context [--candidate] --out=res://.artifacts/<dir>/<id>`. Pass `--candidate` for every species in `f36_pose_candidates.json` `enabled_species`, or it plays the plain clips.
+  - "F36 candidate did not install" in the log means a missing import (re-import) or a stale `source_sha256` pin.
+- **f36 recipes:**
+  - Each profile is one compact JSON line. Edit only that line and validate with `json.loads`.
+  - Never put `_why` keys inside a profile: the loader reads every key as a clip and fails to install. Put notes at the top level instead.
+  - Re-pin `species.<id>.source_sha256` after any GLB byte change, including a texture rewrite.
+- **Texture rewrites** (retex grades, `creature_touch.py`, `shift_reserved_red.py`, `arc_emission.py`):
+  - Rewrite the embedded GLB image and the extracted image.
+  - Re-run `--only vivid <id>` (`repaint_creature_textures.py`) when a vivid PNG exists.
+  - Run `texture_import_policy.py --apply <dir>` for new images, then import again.
+  - The CPU stage self-lights the whole albedo (field_emission), so emission-only changes (arc emission, Tanglevolt field lift) show only on GPU.
+- **Faint end on the stage:** `capture_f36_poses.gd` calls the body's `settle_faint()` at faint-100 (the shipped combat faint settle) and clears it before the next role. Code that measures a seeked pose (`astra_whole_bounds_r4.gd`) must call `force_update_all_bone_transforms()` on the skeletons first, or it reads the previous pose.
+- **Traversal rows with no clip:** `capture_f36_poses.gd` shows what the game plays instead (creature_animator: swim -> walk, ride -> idle; fly_controller: the procedural wingbeat for a `procedural_wing_pose` carrier) and records `runtime_fallback` / `runtime_procedural_wingbeat` in the receipt rather than failing (Galecrest fly_grip, water_cannonback swim/ride).
+- **Ruler clearance in posed frames:** with `--context` the trainer ruler stands `TRAINER_CLEARANCE_M` (1.4 m) clear of each frame's posed body box (`creature_body.gd` `_posed_body_box`), not only the bind-pose box, so a swung tail or rear-back never overlaps the ruler (GPU: Ripplet's tail "crowds the trainer"). Scores from earlier stages carry that artefact for long-tailed species.
+- **Ride row wears the fitted saddle:** mounting always fits the species' saddle in play (`riding_controller.gd` `mount` -> `fit_saddle`), so the `--context` ride row attaches it with `riding_controller._attach_saddle` (water forms use `water_mount_geometry.saddle_offset`) and detaches it after. Earlier ride scores showed a bare back (water_cannonback "perched on the cannons").
+- **Plain captures of enabled species play the recipe:** a species in `f36_pose_candidates.json` `enabled_species` plays its recipe clips in the game (`creature_body.gd` -> `creature_pose_candidates.gd` `install` remaps hit/faint/swim/fly_grip/ride to `f36_candidate/*`). Since 0d2e61ba a plain capture plays them too, so plain equals `--candidate` for those species; plain scores taken before it showed clips the game never plays.
+- **Scale needs a fixed camera:** `--whole-body` frames the camera from each creature's resting box, so growing a creature only shrinks the ruler in frame and judges see no change (b46). Judge scale at the play camera or a fixed-distance stage.
+- **What the CPU stage cannot show:** the BaseMaterial3D rim term and emission (llvmpipe self-lights the albedo). A rim or emission candidate goes straight to GPU with a pixel-diff note, not a CPU judge batch.
+- **Net smokes:** `tools/net/run_net_smoke.sh <name> --out=<dir>` (two peers, about 3 min each); it prints ALL CHECKS PASSED.
+- **Disk recovery:**
+  - A failed fetch leaves `.git/objects/pack/tmp_pack_*` of up to 150 MB; delete it.
+  - Remove `.godot/imported` entries that no `.import` file references.
+  - The classifier refuses `git reset --hard` and `git restore` over work; use `git stash push` instead.
+  - A merge interrupted by a full disk leaves partial copies of the other side's files. Check each against `git hash-object`/`git rev-parse <ref>:<path>` before removing them.
+  - Never `git fetch --depth=N` an asset branch (tb/meshy-1024, tb/creatures) to read a few files: depth 50 of two branches pulled 14 GB. To read files, fetch, `git archive <ref> <paths> | tar -x -C <scratch>`, then delete the remote refs and the new pack and put `.git/shallow` back to HEAD's line.
+  - To post a lane NOTE line on another branch without its blobs: `git fetch --depth=1 --filter=blob:none origin <branch>`, `git hash-object -w` the edited note, then build the commit with a temporary `GIT_INDEX_FILE` (`read-tree`, `update-index --cacheinfo`, `write-tree`, `commit-tree -p origin/<branch>`) and push `<sha>:refs/heads/<branch>`. It costs under 1 MB.
+
 **CPU judging (the `visual-judge` yardstick)**
 1. **Contact sheets:** 2×2 per side at 640×360 per tile. Write a spec `[{label, a, b, brief, defects}]`.
 2. **Judge folder:** `python3 tools/visual_judge/anchor_tiles.py --out <judge dir> --key <outside>/key.json --candidates spec.json --pairs 3 --seed <new each batch> --include craft`. Then copy `docs/reference` into `<judge dir>/reference`; the tool does not.
